 ## Background
-The method was presented in the paper "FROM VOLUME SPLATTING TO RAYCASTING - A Smooth Transition" [S1, unofficial]. It builds on earlier work in volume splatting [Splatting and Point-based Rendering](4975-splatting-and-point-based-rendering.md) and raycasting. The hierarchical representation uses an octree structure as in Laur and Hanrahan (1991) [S1, unofficial]. The pre-integrated classification scheme relies on Engel et al. (2001) [S1, unofficial], and the approximation for variable segment lengths uses Roettger et al. (2000) [S1, unofficial]. The visual variation metric is inspired by Meissner et al. (2000) [S1, unofficial].
+The method was presented in the paper "FROM VOLUME SPLATTING TO RAYCASTING - A Smooth Transition" [S1, unofficial]. It builds on earlier work in volume splatting [Splatting and Point-based Rendering](4975-splatting-and-point-based-rendering.md) and raycasting [S1, unofficial]. The hierarchical representation uses an octree structure as in Laur and Hanrahan (1991) [S1, unofficial]. The pre-integrated classification scheme relies on Engel et al. (2001) [S1, unofficial], and the approximation for variable segment lengths uses Roettger et al. (2000) [S1, unofficial]. The visual variation metric is inspired by Meissner et al. (2000) [S1, unofficial].
 
